t(21, 590, """Divorced women in Muslim society, amid the decline of sound thinking in most societies, have come to need a public body (a marriage office) that matches them with prospective husbands according to regulations and controls that guarantee the soundness of the process from beginning to end. Divorced women in Muslim society have the right to a new beginning.""")

t(21, 1630, """Ordering artificial intelligence to draw pictures is not a kind of detachment from reality .. But if a person has no knowledge of the unseen about how this reality will change, he will remain lost and astray, understanding nothing .. Days ago someone said of the pictures I ordered artificial intelligence to draw that this is conjecture! This is not conjecture .. This is a vision, not a dream .. This is certainty in Allah Almighty, not daydreams. Important note: the Ummah is heading, Allah Almighty willing, toward an overflow of wealth .. And the wealth is not the property of the people of Bayt al-Maqdis. It is the wealth of the whole Ummah .. and the wealth of all the Ummah's great cities .. So, as a person who gives glad tidings of that future by the power of Allah Almighty, relying on the texts and the true visions by the power of Allah our Mighty Lord, I do not give glad tidings to the people of Bayt al-Maqdis alone, Allah Almighty willing.""")

t(22, 2300, """A great psychological collapse in the future of humanity, west and east .. Not today or tomorrow .. but let us say the future .. A great psychological collapse for sick souls that grew used to valuing people by colour, race, nationality, passport, appearance and looks. Those who grew used to practising their psychological illnesses in the days of (their might): some of them will commit suicide, some will be struck by hallucinations, some will be struck by severe depression and will not leave the house, and some will bang their heads against the wall, even those who belong to a single race.""")

t(23, 160, """Quality of life, in the invention of Western management science as a modern term, relates to the quality of life of employees inside their institutions, through adopting a number of regulating standards and measures that achieve quality of life inside the workplace, and linking that to the reflections of the quality of working life on the extent of psychological well-being inside and outside the workplace. The truth is that all this Western (gimmick) is not surprising; in the last twenty-five years we have grown used to finding the West inventing many management theories. In truth they are weighty and have value at the level of theorising, but the West itself failed to implement them so that they would become a reality beyond doubt; it only laid the foundations and the systems for governing the theory and its applications. Then savage Western capitalism (global in its impact) came and said to the scholars of management: Did you believe yourselves?!

Quality of life in the Islamic concept can be stopped by nothing but Western capitalism, for it is the greatest challenge to achieving quality of life for residents according to an Islamic perspective that takes into account the change in man's mind, his thought and his way of looking at things, and that adapts all development initiatives so that they become implementable within the framework of the governance of the virtuous city.

The governance of the virtuous city is extremely easy in some aspects, and extremely complex and intertwined in others. Moving the economy from the dominance of Western theory, which exhausts the human soul, to the justice of Islamic truths, whose ability to correct man's social and psychological course is beyond doubt: this move is very possible, on condition that the tools of imperial dominance of Western theory are absent.

The quality of life of residents in the moderate Islamic model is not limited to institutional quality in the work environment; rather it is an integrated quality covering all the elements of professional, family and social life. It is a quality that takes into account the need of today's man, Muslim and non-Muslim: his need for joy after 100 years of great distress that struck humanity because of Western theory and its imposition on the world by force.

The world needs to breathe, and true (moderate) Islam, with its exemplary intellectual leadership unprecedented in any previous heavenly legislative order, this true (moderate) Islam is capable of making a society that smiles, laughs and rejoices, by standards that guarantee the conditions of the virtuous city whose foundations Islam laid.""")

t(23, 1190, """Everyone who looks at the people of sins and mistakes of all kinds on the new media sites with a look of revulsion and disgust must remember the number of his own sins and mistakes in his life .. No gallows should be set up for anyone .. Today's observant person perhaps was not observant before! Even one who has been observant since childhood: that does not mean he never committed any sins! It is not right and not fitting to despise one who commits mistakes and sins and to look down on him, so that a person puffs himself up and says: Praise be to Allah, I am pious, I am pure, I am an angel, I am a prophet, I am no less than the messengers and prophets, and these sinners are less than me! This is wrong! A person cannot guarantee his steadfastness, nor be sure his foot will stay firm on the path of Allah, the Mighty, the Merciful, the Accepter of repentance.

The people of sins are a model of what we used to be. Not necessarily a complete model of what we used to be. Not necessarily that we did what they do; what is meant by model is that we are something of what they are today. Whether that something was identical or similar, 50% or 30% or 10% or 1%, it does not matter. What matters is that we were not born prophets and did not live our lives as infallible prophets. This is what we must never forget. Those who commit sins and disobedience remind us of those meanings so that, first, we take heed and do not become deluded and arrogant and say: Who is like us today? Who resembles us today? And second, so that we fear, keep fearing and tremble lest Allah Almighty punish us by making us like them, or even worse than them, while He guides them and keeps them firm on guidance, putting us in their place and them in ours as a punishment for us. They remind us that one day we were not what we are today. One day we did not resemble what we are today, and that humility and not bullying them is a sign of guidance; as for bullying those who are not guided, it has nothing to do with guidance, and it is the behaviour of the unguided.""")

t(23, 1885, """Visitors of Jerusalem""")

t(24, 320, """A typo, dear friends: at dawn today I wrote in a post: Please write a comment 😀 instead of writing Please do not write a comment .. My apologies to you; an apology is due""")

t(24, 670, """This post is not about the vision channels

There are two kinds of students of Shari'ah knowledge, its pioneers, the specialists in its sciences and the graduates of its universities .. One kind has done well, and perfection belongs to Allah Almighty alone: it has handled the sciences of the End Times well and gone deep into them. I do not think that among all the channels of End Times sciences there is a channel to be relied upon, as I said, and perfection belongs to Allah Almighty, other than the Basa'ir channel, which has points for it and against it. Personally I disagree with its owner on several issues, and everyone is free in his understanding of Allah Almighty and His Messenger. Apart from Basa'ir, they are gatherers of wood by night who mixed truth with much falsehood and much falsehood with truth; some of them have vanished and their mention has died out, and some are still waiting. But for a person to specialise in Shari'ah knowledge and memorise the rulings of prayer, fasting, hajj, the lawful and the unlawful and all the rulings of Islam does not mean that he will understand the sciences of the End Times, or grasp enough of them for his word to be relied upon in knowledge and understanding. For I see some of those who graduated from Shari'ah faculties not knowing their elbow from their wrist in this science and this art, and they have come out with calamities and oddities, because they think the science of the End Times is a science built only on memorising the hadiths that speak of the End Times. Being in that state, they did not realise how far this many-branched science is not text alone, but also reflection, understanding and drawing the meanings out of the depths of the texts of sound chain. Since they neither did this well nor mastered it, and understood nothing at all about interpreting visions, it was wholly hidden from them. Perhaps they never had a real spiritual connection with heaven, because they were not made fit for that as many men and women were. In that state they crammed themselves into the affairs of the End Times and came out with laughable things fit to be jokes, not knowledge. My advice to these is to return to what they were made fit for and are good at: the sciences of the rulings of the Shari'ah, which people need every day and night. As for the issues of the End Times, they are not issues that rest on memorising the Book and the Sunnah. The matter of End Times issues in particular has nothing to do with memorising the Book and the Sunnah by heart, nor with understanding the rulings of prayer, fasting, hajj, umrah and inheritance .. These people understood the matter wrongly and did not discern the root of this momentous and precious science. Today there are many followers on this channel and other channels who did not study Shari'ah knowledge, yet they understand and grasp a great deal of the sciences of the End Times. The reason for that is that the issues of the End Times are issues of the unseen; this is their broad heading. Those who put themselves forward in the sciences of the End Times without having been granted an opening or made fit for that thorny science only came out with laughable things, because they thought it a science of memorising Qur'an and hadiths only, and forgot that its name is (the science of the unseen): what came in the Book of Allah Almighty, with reflection and understanding, and what came with sound and good chains in the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, with a crown of understanding and insight added to it. If that is not attained and present, the door will never be opened to one who is content with memorising the Qur'an and the Sunnah. As for the top of the crown, it is seeing the Prophet ﷺ in a vision, whose role in explaining and clarifying the knowledge that perplexed people is denied only by an ignorant, pretentious, stubborn-minded, thick-headed person.""")

t(24, 1795, """To the brothers who have illnesses, who suffer and are in pain .. Illness is a trial and a test for the believer. Some of our brothers and sisters suffer from psychological ailments only, some from physical ones only, and some from both psychological and physical together, and they find that they cannot bear it. This is natural, for the soul is neither iron nor a lifeless object, and it is no wonder that it is struck by exhaustion and fatigue. It is no crime that they are in pain, and no crime that they cry for help to Allah the Mighty, our Lord, sanctified be His names, to rescue them, heal them and lift it from them. But I would like to say a word to them, as brief as possible, not so that they stop praying to Allah the Mighty, our Lord, for relief .. Allah forbid .. but so that they stop the complaining between themselves and their own souls .. There is a difference between complaining to Allah and complaining to yourself .. Then you move on to a bad stage, which is complaining to people! You may happen to speak of your pain for a reason that called for disclosure, but how great is the difference between disclosing for a reason, as when you have an appointment and do not go and so you say: I feel very tired; this is not complaining to people; and there being no reason that calls for disclosure while you keep saying: Allah Almighty has afflicted me with such and such! As for seeking advice, it is not complaining to people, as when you seek advice on treating a psychological pain or an organic pain; this too is fine, and it is not of the kind where you complain of Allah to people, Allah forbid .. Complaining of Allah to people is persisting in complaining of what has befallen you, so that it becomes your habit in life, every day or every week or every now and then, to sit with people and say: Allah has afflicted me with such and such. This is the kind where you complain of your Lord to people, Allah forbid.

As for those of our brothers and sisters who do not grasp right and wrong in understanding this issue, I say: the cause of falling into the error of complaining of Allah to people without a justifying reason, such as explaining the reason for an absence or the reason for not carrying out a certain responsibility; falling into that error, which I find great in its size, is caused by not grasping an important issue that we must understand, namely the issue of trial, its duration and its reality.

When a trial occurs, it may last a second or a minute, it may last ten years, and it may last twenty years or more, and so on. The mistake a person may fall into is chasing the trial, so that every day in which he is granted life anew he meets his day with (when): When will this matter end? When will relief come from what I am in? This chasing between you and yourself is natural and there is no harm in it, but it becomes harmful when it causes resentment to arise in your heart against the decree of Allah Almighty, even between you and yourself. This is never permissible. Here you did not stop at merely feeling tired, which is allowed, natural and without harm; rather you went beyond that to resentment at what Allah Almighty wills for you.""")

t(25, 150, """Relief from a trial has never been by the decision of the one tried! The trial does not befall you by your decision, nor does relief come about and take place by your decision! How many a man and a woman, each stricken with a hard and serious illness, went to the hospital after one charity or several charities and were told: There is nothing wrong with you?! How many a sick person did Allah Almighty heal after one particular ruqyah, although he had perhaps been given ruqyah dozens of times before it and was not healed?

The stories of righteous men and women of different degrees are many .. Do not think that these stories are confined only to the miracles of the prophets .. The stories of healing are many; even one of little righteousness may be healed, and the righteous one need not be perfectly righteous .. One who is on the path of Allah may be healed even if he has not yet reached the end of the path .. Healing from a psychological or organic illness may be withheld even from a righteous man! As we see, the cases are many, and when we understand these cases we will realise that a trial is not lifted by complaining, nor by grumbling at it and being weary of it; otherwise no one would be worn out. Not to mention that this behaviour is in the first place behaviour that angers Allah Almighty. You do not know when your ailment will be lifted from you; it may be lifted suddenly. You are not consulted about the ailment coming upon you, nor about its lifting. I remember, 14 years ago, when I was not walking the path of our Lord in the same way and to the same degree as today, my right knee was hurting me for an incomprehensible reason, and the matter stayed like that for months. Satan had made me forget to pray to Allah Almighty to heal me, but the Mighty Lord favoured, bestowed, had mercy, gave, was gentle and blessed. One night, in a vision, there were two doctors wearing white doctors' coats; one of them was holding a health file, which was my health file, and the second doctor was asking the one carrying the file: What is wrong with him? The one carrying the file said: Air has entered his knee. The vision ended and I woke from my sleep and the pain had disappeared completely. Was I consulted about the healing? The answer is no. So however much you hasten the healing, the matter is not by your hastening. And when you keep remembering your ailment, you may not be healed. I remember, 11 years ago, in a vision, 3 angels came down; they were above my body while I was asleep, turning my body over, and I was not cooperating with them. They grew weary of me and of my lack of cooperation and response and went up to heaven. This is the state of one who keeps remembering his ailment but was not healed, even though noble angels came down to treat him .. The stories of people are many .. How many a person saw an angel treating him? Many people .. And how many a person did the Prophet ﷺ come to and wipe over the place of his illness, and Allah Almighty healed him? Many people.

So your complaining or not complaining neither brings forward nor delays your relief from your distress, your worry and your illness. You are required to be patient .. Your forgetting your illness does not keep your healing from you if Allah Almighty wills it for you, and your remembering your ailment between you and yourself .. such as a possession that has exhausted and worn you out, for example, as happened to me 11 years ago .. this remembering will not necessarily result in your healing!

This is a statement and clarification so that clarity of understanding is attained, ignorance of the matter is removed, and mind and awareness are disciplined.""")

t(25, 1345, """Wealth will overflow by the power of our Mighty Lord, sanctified be His names, exalted in the heavens and on earth and high above all with great highness, as the Prophet ﷺ foretold by revelation and notification from his Lord, sanctified be His names .. Wealth will overflow until it will not be known what can be done with it, to the point that it will be scooped out by the handful and not counted! This is something that has never happened before in the human history we know .. Some comment, saying: This is too much .. commenting on the pictures .. But I would like to explain to them so that they understand the picture of what is coming and adapt to what is coming, Allah willing .. The volume of the wealth coming in the future is an unprecedented volume .. and unprecedented quantities .. These are the 7 years of hardship that will strike the whole world (construction workers will be unemployed by the tens of millions), except one single nation in all the earth that this hardship will not strike .. It is the nation of the Muslims .. The nation of the Muslims that has suffered poverty in its outlying regions since the era of the conquests, after Imam Ali, peace be upon him, and al-Faruq, may Allah be pleased with him, when the outlying regions and the centre entered into poverty, except for the period of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz .. It is a nation that has lived in poverty, centre and outlying regions, for no less than 1350 years, and in very many periods even the centre, meaning the capital of the state, Damascus or Baghdad or Fatimid Cairo or even Istanbul .. Even in the capitals, not all their people obtained their rights .. In the last 9 years of the stage before the last for our Ummah, before the Dajjal and then the descent of the Prophet of Allah Isa, peace be upon him, wealth will overflow until it will not be known what can be done with it because of its overflow; for the Prophet ﷺ used the word "overflows", which is from flooding, and he ﷺ did not say "will increase" .. Allah willing, cities, urban centres and dwellings will be built, and there will not remain in the Ummah a hungry or wretched person, or a Muslim man or woman with a worldly need they are unable to meet. Then wealth will still keep overflowing, copious and plentiful, like rain that never ceases! This is the picture of what is coming, which unfortunately 99% of the sons of the Ummah are ignorant of and know nothing about.""")

t(26, 465, """In a disciplined society it is unimaginable that an orphan child be placed with a family without follow-up and reassurance about the child's condition""")

t(26, 1470, """Good morning from the flower of cities .. where there is a people and residents who, when morning comes, greet their day with copies of the Qur'an .. {"And Allah prevails over His affair, but most people do not know"}""")

t(26, 2465, """Commanding and forbidding have states and kinds .. It is not a command when you give advice that holds some benefit with kindness, gentleness and affection; that is neither command nor prohibition. The father whose heart is filled with mercy is neither commanding nor forbidding when his advice grows stern; the mother, when she knows what is good for her son and her advice grows stern, is neither commanding nor forbidding; the sister, when she seeks good for a sister of hers or a brother, is neither commanding nor forbidding when the sincerity of her love is perceived, so no tone of command is seen in her spoken command when it grows stern, nor a tone of prohibition in her spoken prohibition when it grows stern; nor is the tender brother commanding or forbidding in his speech when it grows stern, once the sincerity""")

t(27, 150, """of meaning is perceived from his heart, so that his word is taken as from a sincere, loving person. So too the wife, once the station of her good manners has been settled in her conduct for a time; so too the husband, once the station of his good companionship has been settled for a time; and so too the friend and the neighbour.

If only everyone in our lives truly loved us and so advised us with the advice of one who commands and forbids, life would then be light and easy. Then let them command and let them forbid, for upon our hearts the command would be like honey cleared of every impurity. Even so, let each of us search his life, and he will find that Allah the Mighty, his Lord, has provided him with one of these, or two, or three, or fewer or more.""")

t(27, 575, """Islam is a religion to which people deserve to be called in a place worthy of it .. These are symbolic pictures in which artificial intelligence may overdo the ornamentation .. But the spirit of the places remains important even if the ornamentation in them is less""")

t(27, 1590, """Will the Jerusalem that man has known throughout history remain with the same face and appearance?""")

t(28, 1110, """Restoring the standing of paper and pen once again""")

t(28, 2030, """If this scene were to be for one single day in which people are blessed, from Marrakesh to Karachi and from Istanbul to Aden and Khartoum, it would suffice us that the Muslims lived a share of the world's time and saw the beauty of all that their Lord bestowed on them, of wealth, food, nature, fine dwelling and needs fulfilled, and then departed to their Lord. Perhaps they will be asked, and Allah our Lord alone knows best: "Were you deprived, O My latter servants of the last ones, of anything in the world before you stood before Me?" And they will say: "No, O our Lord. You gave us what You did not give those who came before us, and You were generous to us in giving, as a favour from You and not as a right of ours, with what those before us were not blessed with" .. And I say, while some are apprehensive and doubtful about this matter, having grown used to everything ugly in the life of this world and found it to be the norm settled in their understanding, I say: What do you think of the Lord of the worlds? As for me, what I publish to people is only part of what I think of the Lord of the worlds. So whoever wishes, let him think of his Lord poverty, lowliness and humiliation; and whoever wishes, let him think of his Lord beauty, loftiness and honour.""")

t(29, 835, """I would like to clarify a very serious issue in the reality of humanity today, and at the level of the soundness and health of people's thinking. There is a catastrophic, destructive belief widespread among people today and in every age and time, Muslims and non-Muslims, which in brief is: mercy, not justice. They imagine that they are merciful: they show mercy to people, to animals, to birds, and even to the environment of water, trees and stones, while they are far from justice, and so they think the value of mercy is separate from the value of justice. You find a person saying: I am merciful, yet he is an oppressor! He says: My heart is full of mercy toward people, while he wrongs people, or sides with an oppressor who wrongs people, backs him, props him up and supports him. The first thing in this matter is the illusion of mercy, and the second is detachment from reality. Many merciful ones show mercy to animals and show no mercy to man, and their number today is great. And many merciful ones who imagine that they possess the value of mercy show mercy only to those people they love, but make those they do not love taste kinds of torment. Here the value of justice does not exist. When the value of fairness and justice is absent, the value of mercy becomes imagined, supposed to be realised while it is not realised. How can I be merciful, possessing this value, when I do not possess the value of justice?! This is so we know that the absence of the value of justice and fairness categorically negates a person's possession of the value of mercy, and the value of mercy in him becomes merely imagined and not real. He thinks he is merciful, but he shows mercy to those he loves and torments those he does not love; he is just with those he loves and wrongs those he does not love, and he says: I am merciful to those I love. If he reviewed the value of mercy in himself he would find it fragmented; he would find that he practises the value of mercy only with those he loves! This is not practising the value of mercy; this is practising the behaviour of discrimination, or the behaviour of partisanship for a thing or a person. If a person is partisan to his children and shows mercy to them and not to others, he does not possess the value of mercy! And if he is partisan to his oppressive friend and backs him and says: I showed mercy to my friend, this is not real merciful behaviour, and it is not possession of the value of mercy. Such behaviour has nothing to do with the value of mercy; it is only partisanship for one's kind, one's class, one's like, for lineage and blood, for the friend, and so on. For the quality of justice is absent from that person's behaviour, and the absence of the quality of justice has made the value of mercy in him imagined; he only imagines that he is merciful. The matter is mere illusion and imagining.""")

t(29, 1700, """The doctrine of the Third Great War is not the doctrine of ((the great states occupying each other's lands)), as happened in the occupation and partition of Germany, the occupation of Japan, and before that Japan's occupation of China and East Asia and Hitler's occupation of Europe .. The Third Great War has new strategies, because man's mind has changed .. The English, the French, the Dutch, the Spanish, the Portuguese and others formerly believed, according to the context of the international politics of the era before the First World War, that direct military occupation was the only available means of controlling the economy, because the industrial economy was built on standards unlike today's standards. Hence the macro-economy in every country, and the world economy as a whole, had pillars that required a military landing on the ground, because dominance over resources was the key to economic dominance, industrial or agricultural .. But after direct military occupation proved the reality of its high cost, after political thought developed in the man of the post-Second World War era, and after manufacturing came to rest on wholly new structural pillars and a different philosophy, man no longer sees direct military dominance as the sole key to economic dominance. So the great powers today have come to see that the outcome of any global battle will swing between two basic factors for their coming dominance: the first, reducing to zero the manufacturing, agricultural and service capacity of the rival enemy; the second, on the basis of that reduction to zero, imposing a new policy on the defeated great power, so that it sells its precious minerals under compulsion and duress in return for relief for its people, the power of whose dominant state has fallen. All of this does not require a strategic landing by the victorious state in order to set up a direct military occupation authority; the presence of high commissioners in the decision-making centre of the defeated great power is enough!

So the great powers today do not desire or want to occupy one another militarily, because they believe that, from their point of view, global dominance over the economy in the future cannot be achieved at low cost and with less effort except by smashing the manufacturing capacities that each power has reached. This means that landing by land amid hundreds of millions of people and risking soldiers, as happened in Vietnam and elsewhere, is no longer a successful or useful thing.

This new conception of the way to dominate the world is dangerous, because this new model of colonial thought, based on zero direct military occupation, is what in the end pushes toward the comprehensive and wide-scale smashing of the manufacturing machine, with all its components, of every side. Unfortunately, as analysis and foresight, I say that this is the coming shape and form of the Great World War. Therefore the strikes will be concentrated mainly on the industrial cities and on the sectors of energy, communications, airports and ports, and all the joints of the great state. Therefore the idea of nuclear strikes, though it seems remote, still stands; but there are many options under a definite offensive ceiling by which""")

t(30, 150, """everyone can avoid total destruction, by setting definite rules of engagement and abiding by them; but if one side breaches them, the door will be open to expanding the destructive force.""")

t(30, 445, """Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Thaqafi, conqueror of India, in the year 93 AH! His cousin al-Hajjaj sent him to India to conquer it when he was 18 years old. He died in his prison in Iraq, where he had been brought from India to Iraq bound in chains and humiliated, because of a personal dispute between the caliph in Damascus and his cousin al-Hajjaj; it was a personal dispute with which Muhammad ibn al-Qasim had nothing to do. So the Umayyad caliph halted the conquests of Islam in India, punished a person who had nothing to do with his personal problems with al-Hajjaj, merely because of the tie of kinship between al-Hajjaj and Muhammad ibn al-Qasim, and deprived people of Islam spreading among them!""")

t(30, 1620, """Some of our brothers, when they see pictures like these, are struck by fatigue and exhaustion, merely from seeing the picture! Their souls have become too tight for them from the worldly hardship they have lived, their resolve has become weak and their souls slack, and they tire even from the mere idea! At once they remember the dust, the stones, the sun, the sweat and the effort! This happens to souls that have no capacity and in which the capacity found in other souls has not been widened.""")

